# Urdais environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development. `.env.local` and other
# real environment files are git-ignored; never commit secrets.
#
# Variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are inlined into the browser bundle.
# Server-only secrets must NOT use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.

# --- Application ---------------------------------------------------------
# Public origin of the web app (no trailing slash). Used for absolute URLs
# and metadata. Defaults to http://localhost:3000 when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=

# --- Supabase (development backend) ---------------------------------------
# The hosted development project is UrdaisDev. Its project reference is not a
# secret: it appears in every public API URL for the project. The Supabase CLI
# records the same reference in the git-ignored supabase/.temp/ after
# `supabase link`. Everything else below is a secret and lives only in
# .env.local or the shell, never in git.
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=scwwjoyouohfrwylalha
#
# Needed only by whoever applies migrations to the hosted project by CLI
# (`supabase db push`). PR CI never uses it and never touches UrdaisDev.
#   SUPABASE_DB_PASSWORD=
#
# --- Supabase Auth (required for sign-in; Paid Access Phase 2) -------------
# Both are public by design and are inlined into the browser bundle. Without
# them Urdais runs exactly as it did before authentication existed: every
# reader is anonymous and every public product works. Nothing breaks; there is
# simply no way to sign in.
#
# The project API origin. Not a secret.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://scwwjoyouohfrwylalha.supabase.co
#
# The *publishable* key (sb_publishable_…), from Settings > API Keys. Not the
# legacy `anon` JWT: Supabase retires the legacy keys at the end of 2026, and
# src/lib/auth/config.ts rejects one rather than working until that date.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_…
#
# --- Premium enforcement (Paid Access Phase 3) -----------------------------
# The commercial activation switch for the premium gate system. Server-only: it
# is deliberately NOT a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, and no query parameter, cookie or
# header can override it.
#
# Leave it UNSET in production. The gates for Compute Economics, Power Analytics
# and the three premium map layers are fully implemented and inactive; unset
# means production serves those products exactly as it always has.
#
# The only value that switches enforcement on is the exact string "active".
# Anything else -- "true", "1", "on", a typo -- reads as inactive, so a mistake
# cannot paywall the live site.
#
# Set it in a preview or development environment to verify the gates:
#   URDAIS_PREMIUM_ENFORCEMENT=active
#
# Do not set it in production until Stripe checkout exists, onboarding replaces
# /access, and an operator can grant a manual entitlement. Until then an
# activated gate would show every visitor "Get Full Access" with no way to buy
# it. See docs/architecture/premium-gates.md.

# --- Premium audience onboarding (Phase 8) -------------------------------
# Server-only HMAC key for the short-lived cookie that carries an optional
# audience category through passwordless authentication. Use at least 32 random
# characters and the same value across all instances in one deployment.
#   URDAIS_ONBOARDING_STATE_SECRET=

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY (the legacy JWT) is NOT used and should not be set.
# Urdais reaches Postgres through `pg` on DATABASE_URL, and identity and
# entitlement reads run on that privileged connection.
#
# --- Supabase Auth administration (server-only; Phase 7D) -------------------
# The modern secret key (sb_secret_…, Settings > API Keys), used for ONE thing:
# `auth.admin.deleteUser` when a reader deletes their account
# (src/lib/auth/admin.ts). Never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never logged, never used for
# application data. Without it, account deletion reports itself unavailable
# BEFORE doing anything -- it never cancels billing and then stalls. Use the
# key of the SAME project as NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL (UrdaisDev locally,
# UrdaisProd only in Vercel Production).
#   SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_…
#
# Token-price catalog (server-only). `loadTokenReadCatalog()` reads
# pipeline.token_price_observations. In `next dev`, if unset, the loader
# uses the local harness URL from `scripts/db/local.sh url`
# (postgresql://postgres@localhost:54329/urdais_local). Production never
# uses that default and never publishes research-only rows.
#   DATABASE_URL=
#   URDAIS_DATABASE_URL=

# --- Supabase (production backend) -----------------------------------------
# The hosted production project is UrdaisProd. It is a separate database from
# UrdaisDev and is never a copy of it: its migration history was applied from
# zero, and the only rows it holds beyond schema seeds are manually verified
# production observations. The reference is not a secret, for the same reason
# the development one is not.
SUPABASE_PRODUCTION_PROJECT_REF=cyqtaydtfuwaexjkuynq
#
# A deployed instance needs DATABASE_URL pointing at UrdaisProd, and nothing
# else. Two things about that string are easy to get wrong:
#   - use the session pooler (aws-0-us-east-1.pooler.supabase.com:5432, user
#     postgres.<ref>). The direct db.<ref>.supabase.co host is IPv6-only.
#   - Supabase presents its own certificate authority, so a default
#     verify-full fails. Download the project CA from the dashboard and append
#     sslmode=verify-full&sslrootcert=<path>.
# NODE_ENV=production is what selects the fail-closed production read path.
# See docs/operations/production-environments.md.
#   DATABASE_URL=
#
# The serverless *read* path does not connect with that string verbatim. A
# session-pooler URL is moved to the transaction pooler's port (6543) on the
# same host, because the session pooler allots about fifteen clients to the
# whole role and a handful of concurrent Vercel instances can take all of them,
# at which point every production-backed read on the site goes empty at once.
# The cron routes and the migration/admin tooling keep the string as written.
# Nothing else about the URL changes, TLS parameters included.
#   URDAIS_DATABASE_RUNTIME_URL=
#
# Optional, and only to override that: set it to name the serverless read
# path's connection string explicitly. Leave it unset unless the derived one is
# wrong for your topology.

# --- UCPI collector runtime (server-only; no value here is ever committed) --
# Read only by src/lib/ucpi/runtime/config.ts, and only at run time. The
# runtime refuses production or validation retrieval when a source is not
# production-approved in the registry, when no permission grant is in force,
# or when the credential below is absent. Simulation mode needs none of these.
#
# Run mode: simulation (default; fixtures only, no network) | validation
# (live credentialed retrieval, evidence only, never publishes) | production.
UCPI_RUN_MODE=simulation
#
# Documented API hosts. Configuration, not assumptions; confirmed at first
# authenticated validation. The registry records the Runpod catalog under
# https://api.runpod.io and the Lambda instance types under https://cloud.lambda.ai.
#   UCPI_RUNPOD_BASE_URL=https://api.runpod.io
#   UCPI_LAMBDA_BASE_URL=https://cloud.lambda.ai
#   UCPI_PRICE_OF_COMPUTE_BASE_URL=https://priceofcompute.com   (keyless; 1,000 requests/day; attribution required)
#
# Provider API keys. Server-only. Never logged, never in errors, never here.
#   RUNPOD_API_KEY=
#   LAMBDA_API_KEY=

# --- Scheduled news ingestion (server-only) --------------------------------
# Vercel Cron calls /api/cron/news on the Urdais news cadence (daily, capped by
# the plan; see src/lib/news/schedule.ts) and sends this value as an
# `Authorization: Bearer <secret>` header. The route refuses every request that
# does not match, and refuses all of them when the variable is unset, so an
# unconfigured deployment has no open ingestion trigger rather than a public
# one. Use a random string of at least 16 characters. Set it in the Vercel
# project, not here; the value never belongs in git.
#   CRON_SECRET=
#
# The same route needs DATABASE_URL pointing at UrdaisProd (see above). Without
# it the route answers 503 and ingests nothing.

# --- UTVI source: OpenRouter Datasets API (research only) ----------------
# Any valid OpenRouter API key authenticates the public datasets endpoints;
# the same key used for inference works. Published limits are 30 requests per
# minute per key and 500 per day per account.
#
#   OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# --- Power Delivery / EIA Form 930 (server-only) ----------------------------
# Free EIA Open Data API key used by the hourly PD-2 collector. The key is sent only to
# api.eia.gov and is removed from the request URL retained as provenance.
#   EIA_API_KEY=
#
# Used today only by scripts/research/utvi-characterize-openrouter.ts, which is
# read-only and not wired into the application. No production code reads it and
# no UTVI ingestion exists yet; see docs/research/utvi/source-characterization.md.
# The returned data is CC BY 4.0 and every published value must carry
# "Source: OpenRouter (openrouter.ai/rankings), as of {as_of}."

# --- Contact form delivery (server-only) ----------------------------------
# POST /api/contact sends the footer contact form to the Urdais inbox through
# Resend (src/lib/contact/delivery.ts). All three are server-only: never
# NEXT_PUBLIC_, never logged. With any of them unset the form still renders,
# but Send reports "Something went wrong" and the route logs which names are
# missing (names only, never values).
#
# SECRET. A Resend API key with sending access. A key restricted to the
# sending domain below is enough.
#   RESEND_API_KEY=re_...
#
# NON-SECRET but private: the inbox that receives contact messages. Read only
# on the server, so it never reaches the browser bundle.
#   CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=
#
# The From address. Must be on a domain verified in Resend (SPF and DKIM DNS
# records). The reader's own address is used only as Reply-To, never as From.
# A display name is allowed, e.g. "Urdais Contact <contact@urdais.com>".
#   CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=

# --- Product analytics (PostHog) -------------------------------------------
# Both PUBLIC by design and inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time, so a
# change needs a redeploy. Without either one, analytics is simply off: nothing
# is sent and nothing breaks. `next dev` and tests never send, whatever is set.
#
# Set these in Vercel's PRODUCTION scope only. Preview deployments are production
# builds too, and would otherwise report preview traffic as real visitors.
# See docs/architecture/analytics.md.
#
# Before setting them, enable "Cookieless server hash mode" in the PostHog
# project (Settings > Web analytics). Visitors who decline analytics are counted
# cookielessly, and without that setting PostHog drops their events.
#
# The PROJECT key (phc_…), from PostHog > Project settings. Never the personal
# API key (phx_…), which administers the organisation; config.ts refuses it.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_…
#
# The project's ingestion host: https://us.i.posthog.com or https://eu.i.posthog.com.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=https://us.i.posthog.com
#
# Erasing a deleted account's analytics (account deletion, the daily
# /api/cron/analytics-erasure, and npm run analytics:erase).
# SECRET: a PostHog *personal* API key scoped to person:write only. Server-only —
# never NEXT_PUBLIC_, never logged, never committed. Set both in Vercel Production
# BEFORE analytics is activated, and keep them for as long as PostHog may hold
# Urdais data: while either PostHog setting is present, account deletions wait at
# `auth_deleted` until PostHog accepts the erasure.
# See docs/operations/posthog-activation.md § Account deletion.
#   POSTHOG_PERSONAL_API_KEY=phx_…
#   POSTHOG_PROJECT_ID=

# --- Future integrations (not wired up yet) ------------------------------
# These sections will be populated when the corresponding slices are built.
# Do not add values here until the integration exists.
#
# Urdais API:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=
#
# Cache (Upstash Redis, server-only):
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
#   UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# --- Stripe subscription billing (Paid Access Phase 5) ---------------------
# Urdais sells one thing: Urdais Premium, $80/week recurring. Checkout is
# Stripe-hosted, so Urdais never sees a card number and holds no PCI surface.
#
# TEST AND LIVE CANNOT BE MIXED. The mode is read from the secret key's own
# prefix (sk_test_ / sk_live_) and checked against the deployment: production
# requires a live key, everything else requires a test key. A mismatch makes
# billing "unavailable" -- the subscription offer renders with no purchase
# control -- rather than selling something that does not exist. See
# src/lib/billing/mode.ts and docs/architecture/stripe-billing.md.

# SERVER-ONLY SECRET. Can spend money and read every customer in the account.
# Never NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never logged, never committed.
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...

# SERVER-ONLY SECRET. Stripe signs webhooks with this; it is the only reason a
# webhook can be trusted to move an entitlement. Obtained per endpoint from
# the Stripe dashboard, or from `stripe listen` for local forwarding.
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# NON-SECRET server configuration. The canonical Urdais Premium Price. Not
# hard-coded in application logic because it differs between test and live.
# Create or reconcile it with `npm run billing:setup`, which prints the id.
#   STRIPE_PREMIUM_PRICE_ID=price_...

# PUBLIC, and currently UNUSED. Checkout is Stripe-hosted and Urdais loads no
# browser Stripe client, so nothing reads this. Kept documented so its presence
# in an environment is not mistaken for a missing integration.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_...
